yaml/string/folded-block
description: A > block — line breaks folded into spaces
- >
  A folded block starts with `>` and reads like the literal one, except single line breaks FOLD
  into spaces — paragraphs for prose; a blank line keeps a real break. It carries the same two
  qualifiers as the literal block: chomping (`>-`, `>+`) and the indentation indicator (`>2`):
- !!<format: text/x-yaml> |
  note: >
    these two lines
    become one
